# Build output. `npm run build` assembles _site/ from publish-allowlist.txt and
# Netlify serves it. Generated on every deploy, never committed.
_site/

# Audit-salvage patch exports (bdb7eff). Netlify published from "." when this
# rule was written, so anything tracked was fetchable live. These three files
# are unreviewed local-work exports — bdb7eff's own message says "ruling
# pending review" — and one is a 2,379-line stash export from the
# initial-commit era. They stay in git history and are recoverable with
# `git show bdb7eff:patches/<name>.patch`; they do not ship.
patches/

# The morgue (Aug 4, 2026). Internal record of KILLED work — retired surfaces,
# their frozen markup, and screenshots of compositions that were decided
# against. netlify.toml has always said "never production"; the rules meant to
# enforce that were [[context.production.redirects]], which Netlify does not
# support and silently ignores, so /morgue/ served 200 on www.wizkoo.com.
# publish = "." made tracked and published the same set, so the only
# categorical exclusion available was to leave the tracked tree. Intact in
# history:
#   git show 47cedd3:morgue/index.html
morgue/

# ── Publish exclusions, Aug 4 2026 ──────────────────────────────────────────
# wizkoo.com publishes _site/, which `npm run build` assembles from the paths
# named in publish-allowlist.txt. THAT FILE DECIDES WHAT SHIPS. Read it to
# find out whether a page is on the website; a file gets there by being named
# in it and by no other route.
#
# These rules are therefore no longer what keeps anything off the site. Not
# being named in the manifest is. They stay as a second layer beneath the
# first, and because keeping local artefacts out of the tracked tree is worth
# doing on its own. Everything below is an internal working record, not a
# page, and was fetchable on production until 9115d7b. All of it stays in git
# history.

# Killed-copy records. Same class as the morgue: copy and surfaces that were
# decided against. History: git show 59ac112:docs/archive/homepage-2026-07-31/KILLED-COPY.md
docs/archive/
docs/copy-refile-son-space-panel.md

# Internal lab and preview surfaces, never linked from the site.
# History: git show 59ac112:lab/orbital.html
lab/
actual-size-preview.html
library/actual-size.html

# Shell-redirect artefacts: a Windows "C:" became C+U+F03A, so the whole path
# became a filename at the repo root. Byte-duplicates of exports/sweep_ids.txt
# and migrations/_tmp_all_ids.txt, which remain tracked.
# Their names begin C + U+F03A (a colon-lookalike). A pattern containing that
# character does NOT match reliably here, so the rule keys on the unmistakable
# embedded path instead: ASCII-only, root-anchored, and impossible to confuse
# with CLAUDE.md or any real page.
/*UsersamyogDesktopWizkoo*

# Tool output, Aug 18 2026. Neither was ignored before this date despite the
# Aug 3 ruling that both "stay untracked" — the ruling was recorded in memory
# and never enforced in the tree. Not published either way: publish-allowlist
# .txt names neither, and that is what decides.
#   .netlify/      Netlify CLI link/state for this machine
#   test-results/  Playwright run output
.netlify/
test-results/
